  <p class=3D"corner-intro">A collection of web design and development news=
 and thoughts from CodePen's own Chris Coyier.</p>=0D=0A                   =
       </mj-raw>=0D=0A                          <p>As of January, with Fire=
fox 147=E2=80=99s release, Anchor Positioning is supported <a href=3D"https=
://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/3koKv3_K1-200ZTT4rE4bQ~~/AABEfhA~/vpyLlK8PmW4q=
zm1YulE8Hs9CWKduqeTiGdo9NPGiZ5rIu69_IhAzJeF_MpM_o4kHaiM49zPeic2_wV9AlW_NvIz=
b9PXsTqzNC192nYeEFOShHV55G4jgssXrqzeyHy0YmA_uvwk3MJ7fH2e6Qnx7ew~~">across a=
ll major browsers</a>.</p>=0A<p>I=E2=80=99m happy about that, of course. I =
think Anchor Positioning is really powerful and a layout mechanism we proba=
bly should have had a long time ago. My enthusiasm was tempered when I foun=
d out how finicky it can, simply <em>not finding</em> anchors for reasons y=
ou have to be somewhat of a web expert to be able to diagnose and fix.</p>=
=0A<p>I wrote all this up in <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/L=
CEAot1l77VWauW6H2HsbA~~/AABEfhA~/HIwZs21uxhVZak2nCf20ja1cjsertUiZrGE6SC6BuR=
25wrZPpgu9mKzupRk-3d8Xnqikhix7dTaxSiwCmwCQog1pOZUE9_2R1E2z5M7Kfj_fpoqOSVFFl=
wAWsQnoqJePhdMa2Y0hUcDEgt9OUHec-xrfXB4bh2OUCCL5cdViwb4m8MPF3EoflzgOvYVD4F14=
">The Big Gotcha of Anchor Positioning</a>, which is something of a rant as=
 if I can be a squeaky wheel that helps makes this better in the future, I=
=E2=80=99m happy to do it. There are some better articles on what is actual=
ly going on and how to deal with it:</p>=0A<ul>=0A<li>Temani Afif: <a href=
=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/K59DsScUbEDUrvFEe_nQgg~~/AABEfhA~/Oxg=
o_dPgtiNpKw5fqYrJ4p3rTE-x4NtPxMoXeHlZZRBHuORnzC1Ns90voNpbMEKGzYbuVh3kAnFtl-=
KIi-lfSs0dUVhCg9154mIZ8A2KCCOK5dp0YRTTjnOhTSXOwAvkUP6ezjqDFETyKX7gy1p68A~~"=
>Why is Anchor Positioning not working</a>=3F</li>=0A<li>James Stuckey Webe=
r: <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/REQIteVHs9ElSvTq--dTaA~~/AA=
BEfhA~/P8K78juAz3wjQ4Usy_3eNPLpy6uCmtzwry__Pw8NPd01YX4ctnh9OyBUWovSpU4ger4T=
CdyWP_9kmZzGALvdBg2l1nmRdSW_JoO13HTDL0APJs6f2PNIWwfceKYiCU00Eh-ywA_O5aYlYOL=
svTFMY3BptpqxKmSp4L2W0qceLNk~">Here=E2=80=99s Why Your Anchor Positioning I=
sn=E2=80=99t Working</a></li>=0A</ul>=0A<p>Articles like that that do a goo=
d technical dive and explain the situation are great, but I wish they didn=
=E2=80=99t have to exist, thus the ranting angle =F0=9F=98=87.</p>=0A<p>Ahm=
ad Shadeed has a typically great post on <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmai=
l2.com/f/a/yfrfJXsqS4jhhWdf9QYgig~~/AABEfhA~/zv7eGg78t7uT_em5N-EiEzU7atpVhD=
1lkE610LpkFHOI0rYPJElkFX-sgLRzfC_3zV8x-LXSdQCZ0A5b8xPVV_W0--2H7GWmDDpnkwSOO=
WBdtNwPsUH4hYv65ztEi6ap1wfEnj7S3DybveOe8CMWfw~~">The Basics of Anchor Posit=
ioning</a> (ugh, that header is so cool). Ahmad walks through a situation (=
placing a badge over an image) that feels very relatable, and anchor positi=
oning is a perfect fit. I would note though (raises hand definantly) that i=
t just so happens the DOM structure works here. If Ahmad had put the =E2=80=
=9Ccard tag=E2=80=9D in the same parent container as the image, which is a =
perfectly reasonable choice, the anchor would just stop working. Figuring o=
ut why that=E2=80=99s broken, unless you=E2=80=99re an avid reader of front=
-end blogs, would be pretty darn difficult.</p>=0A<p>I think it=E2=80=99s n=
otable that <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/kLfBwJCM1dmSTV6n1u=
OtKA~~/AABEfhA~/gy-19-JDEw5X_1Bs2ISzSpvV0ogHexh1zhpNDgueDG6l5CVjl1kZj7Z0Eoy=
6G5B7NeClbVEEcw-zwgV7g6HT0e1LcgjxfYmT5O4y_LDLR_tD2XOCjV0g66tV1fM7iwF3My5EJM=
2rxVt9SWY8Kxkyw_kwTeXjSzjuXGAGPQHxdfCUXElFLaJaNZXezhVJK98f">Anchor Position=
ing is in Interop 2026</a> again. They call that a =E2=80=9Ccarryover=E2=80=
=9D. They say:</p>=0A<blockquote><p><a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.co=
m/f/a/4uVHJs_uDQD1QxBdRJ_t_w~~/AABEfhA~/E7LFz1I6wN56gzMpns2iglStp7567P0WdNK=
dCk475wdLubFatwexv2WSIygsBKy7cw2Ch2Qem5DptZxcFbSlVmN6Uv0fype5hqYEkrUlXGkeCy=
L4o825WweePKFZ9F_yBccMPIK9zyOqagbzqau_6SqDdp66kIiLaZmzBxy5EqldZBwaj6bV5gEuJ=
kIpaumR">Anchor positioning</a> is a carryover from Interop 2025, where sig=
nificant progress was made to empower developers to position elements relat=
ive to each other. This year=E2=80=99s focus will be on clarifying the spec=
, resolving test issues, and increasing the reliability of this powerful la=
yout feature.</p></blockquote>=0A<p>If the spec is still able to be updated=
 a bit, I hope they consider my plea to figure out a way to make resolving =
anchors more resilient.</p>=0D=0A                          =0D=0A          =
